44|null@totalwar^1439811432#3hayxt:DogbertCA$:Total War: ARENA Devs Reddit Q&amp;A
5|0@totalwar^1439825554#cu5y6lh:Gentlemoth$:Are there going to be anything to counterbalance skirmisher kiting like for example, a stamina mechanic?
3|0@totalwar^1439998611#cu8c6y1:DogbertCA$:There are lots of ways to deal with skirmishers kiting melee units in game. On a stamina mechanic We don’t think that either stamina or a walk/run toggle will make the game more fun. It just increases the game’s complexity without adding very much to gameplay, at least for the type of game we’re making. It makes sense in single-player focussed games like classic TW games, but for our more fast-paced online game, it’s just not right. So no, we’re not planning on adding either.
3|0@totalwar^1439923081#cu7btjm:Extradaemon$:I would like it if ammunition was represented too. 
2|0@totalwar^1439998626#cu8c7b1:DogbertCA$:At the moment we’re not planning on adding ammo. We’ve got a system for ammunition in the code, but we feel that this would add unnecessary complexity. In the last patch, archers have been significantly weakened, and we want to see how that plays out in the long term. We’ll continue to watch the game balance and if we feel that ammo is the right solution to create more balance, we’ll add it back in… it’s just that right now we don’t feel that would be the right thing to do.
1|0@totalwar^1440004432#cu8g7ks:unseine$:Then your ranged units become completely useless? Thats not fun. If they every do add that there needs to be a way to get ammo back (probably at base) and a high ammo count.
1|0@totalwar^1440004599#cu8gbzg:Extradaemon$:Yeah, I think having ammo refill at the capturable towers or at base would be a good way to do it, gives more use to the towers too. 
2|0@totalwar^1439825601#cu5y7ll:DETrooper$:Is there an E.T.A. on Patch 11?
3|0@totalwar^1439997297#cu8bc9u:DogbertCA$:We just released Hotfix 10.1. Patch 11 will come in September. :-)
4|0@totalwar^1439831439#cu61to8:dogeofcerberus$:Loving the alpha. Are you getting good feedback from testers? Is there something we can do that helps you more? And Any plans to scale back the exp needed atname higher tiers or scale up the exp gain for killing other high tier units? It seems a bit grindy already at tier 4.
5|0@totalwar^1439997218#cu8baf7:DogbertCA$:The feedback from the community on the forum has been great so far. All I can think is to play and keep telling us what you think. And to answer your question. We’re constantly looking at the progression speed balancing and we’ve already updated it three times since we first launched in November 2014. We need to balance letting people progress without it feeling grindy with giving people enough content to play for several months. At the moment we only have two factions, and it will take you a few months to complete them (depending on how much you play). When we add more factions, we may very well increase the speed at which you progress. Regardless, we’re always looking at our metrics and player feedback and will keep balancing and rebalancing.
0|0@totalwar^1439832170#cu62aon:pewpewfuckinlasers$:When we gonna have that chat you mentioned? This is wolf total war btw ;)
4|0@totalwar^1439822937#cu5woto:Rawrurfaceoff$:Thanks for doing this guys. I'm loving the alpha. What kinds of unit can we expect to see as new factions are released? (Axes?) Are you planning on keeping the maximum party size at 4?
6|0@totalwar^1439996744#cu8azru:DogbertCA$:Axes?? The next faction we’re going to release are the Barbarians. They’re going to play very differently from the Greeks and Romans. Their focus is a lot more on light units, hit-and-run tactics, and fast movement. So you’re going to see a lot of fast units with low armour that can put out a high amount of damage if used right. Not sure if they’ll have axes. 
8|0@totalwar^1439996777#cu8b0jh:DogbertCA$:Party size? We’re looking at our metrics to see what the best party size is. For now, we can’t tell yet. There will be the possibility to have 10v10 custom battles with a lobby in the future, so maybe you won’t need bigger parties then.. 
1|0@totalwar^1440041003#cu93jcl:WalrusJones$:I believe they probably will, given the number of axes listed in the files. Most were listed as being comparable to a Tarantine-Sword.
11|0@totalwar^1439823649#cu5x3c5:WetButler$:* Are there any plans to balance later tier units versus earlier tier units? * Will there ever be stamina or a walk/run toggle? * Any plans for ammo for ranged units?
9|0@totalwar^1439997809#cu8bnwj:DogbertCA$:1.) Yes. We constantly balance the units! In one of the next updates you’ll see T9 and T10 units getting a lot of game design love, and this will also mean that their balance versus earlier units will be affected. 2.) We don’t think that either stamina or a walk/run toggle will make the game more fun. It just increases the game’s complexity without adding very much to gameplay, at least for the type of game we’re making. It makes sense in single-player focussed games like classic TW games, but for our more fast-paced online game, it’s just not right. So no, we’re not planning on adding either. 3.) At the moment we’re not planning on adding ammo. We’ve got a system for ammunition in the code, but we feel that this would add unnecessary complexity. In the last patch, archers have been significantly weakened, and we want to see how that plays out in the long term. We’ll continue to watch the game balance and if we feel that ammo is the right solution to create more balance, we’ll add it back in… it’s just that right now we don’t feel that would be the right thing to do.
2|0@totalwar^1440016808#cu8p5qw:WetButler$:Thank you the insight, Dogbert! For the record, really enjoying the game even in Alpha, and look forward to what's to come.
