7|0@totalwar^1439819740#cu5uzsx:Thepow$:Will there be alternate Battle modi with less players? (dont have to be more units for that, i think) Will there be different scenarios or only base vs base on symetric maps?
6|0@totalwar^1439998374#cu8c18y:DogbertCA$: We feel that 10v10 with three units is just the right balance. It allows individual players to shine and turn the battle around, while at the same time it also allows the team to overcome mistakes by less experiences players. We want to make sure that we balance the right amount of heroism with making it easier for newbies to thrive. The last thing we want is toxic behaviour between players, and this design can help with that. We’ve also already discussed a tournament mode (5v5) internally, and we’ve got several ideas about how to do that. However, we’ll only start a new game mode once we feel that the core game (10v10) is as fun as we want it to be.
2|0@totalwar^1439839201#cu66yqe:anewitguy$:Thank you guys so much for providing such an exciting game to play. Can you tell us a vague vague timeline of what other factions are expected to be released, and in what order? How often should we expect to see new maps? Most importantly, is there any plan to monitor/punish people who try to abuse the queuing system and "afk" through battles regularly?
4|0@totalwar^1439997432#cu8bfbc:DogbertCA$:1.)Barbarians will come this year. Then… we’ll see. ;-) We’re currently considering a variety of factions to come after that, including Late Antiquity factions, Middle Eastern and even Far Eastern factions. 2.) We’re hoping to release a new map roughly every two months or so. However, if a map isn’t good enough in our testing, we’re not releasing it. It’s more important to us to give you good content than to stick to a strict release schedule. We’ve already thrown away a few maps in the process. 3.) Yes. AFK players already no longer receive any rewards. There are also plans for dealing with people who behave badly in other ways. 
1|0@totalwar^1439998502#cu8c4b2:anewitguy$:Thanks for the response on 1 and 2. As far as 3 goes, if an AFK player's troops are engaged by an opponent how does that currently work? Since they are fighting/engaging they would be earning XP still, would they not? In addition, a victorious commander, even if AFK, still would receiving the gold bonus, would they not? Thanks so much!
1|0@totalwar^1440056008#cu99cmw:jvdc$:If an AFK unit is engaged with another player, the AFK unit doesn't earn any XP, but the other player will.
